  "meta": {
    "probe": "ransom-note-b",
    "target": "same target as ransom-note, different object: one word stacked down a whole page on cut strips, rather than a slogan hand-set across the middle",
    "method": "each row is a group with its own translate and rotate, so the strips are cut and laid down independently. Because each strip is a full-width torn polygon rather than a per-letter patch, the letters can be much larger and the tear is a page-width event instead of a decorative edge",
    "notDone": "the tears are still hand-authored polygons -- straight segments, no fibre, no white core. And the two available faces are both Regular, so mismatched weight is faked with size and rotation"
  },
